From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:07:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] app: scroll performance recorder with a share button
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Users report that the library grid sometimes stutters on drag and fling and
sometimes is smooth. They have no adb, Perfetto or network upload, so this
adds a debug switch that records frame timing on the device and writes a
file they can share by hand.

Settings -> Advanced -> "Scroll performance recorder (debug)", preference
key harmony_scroll_perf_recorder, default off. While it is on and
MainActivity is started, HarmonyFramePerf (shared byte for byte with the
sibling app) records into primitive ring buffers allocated on first attach
and dropped when the switch is turned off (about 1 MB):

- FrameMetrics per rendered frame, delivered on its own HandlerThread:
  intended / actual vsync, total, unknown delay, input, animation,
  layout+measure, draw, sync, command issue, swap; GPU and DEADLINE on
  API 31+, -1 otherwise. 6000 frames.
- The Choreographer vsync interval on the main thread (6000 ticks), which
  keeps working when FrameMetrics does not. Each tick carries the panorama
  scroll phase (idle / drag / fling, a volatile in PanoramaScrollTrace set
  at down, up, fling start and fling end), the number and total time of
  PanoramaMasonry measure passes and the number of newly composed cells.
  Those counters live in PanoramaFrameCounters; the hot path is one
  nanoTime pair and additions, no allocation.
- Every 500 ms: GC count delta, process CPU delta, display refresh rate and
  mode, thermal status (API 29+) and battery saver.
- If no frame arrives within 3 s of attach (a frame is forced by
  invalidating the decor view) the export says "FrameMetrics 未提供" and
  the summary uses Choreographer intervals only.

A 40 dp translucent "记录" button sits bottom-start above the bottom
navigation (safeDrawing insets) only while recording; touches elsewhere
pass through. A tap writes "mark user" into the scroll trace, builds
<app>_scroll_perf_<yyyyMMdd-HHmmss>.txt in the cache directory on a
background thread and opens the share sheet like the crash log dump.

The export is built by pure functions (PerfReport) from numbers only:
header (app id, version, brand / model, Android / SDK, window dp, density,
supported and current refresh rate, thermal, battery saver, uptime, start
time); per scroll segment fps, jank count and p50 / p90 / p99 / max frame
time with the dominant stage; jank stage means; Choreographer interval
percentiles and the count over 1.5 vsync; every jank frame and 500 ms
sample of the last 30 s; per-second counts of 卓易通 graphics-layer logcat
lines (HARMONY_NOISE_MARKERS, now internal to CrashLogUtil); and the
PanoramaScrollTrace snapshot. Jank is TOTAL_DURATION > DEADLINE when the
deadline is known, otherwise > 1.5 vsync periods. It never contains logcat
text, titles, URLs, extension list, file paths, accounts or
HarmonyLogBuffer, and ends with
"privacy: no titles, urls, extension list or logcat text".

Cost while on: one FrameMetrics callback per frame off the main thread, a
Choreographer callback every vsync (keeps the main looper waking at the
refresh rate) and a 500 ms sampler. Nothing runs while the switch is off.

